.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.TH OCTA-PULSE-PAIRS 1 "" "OCTA-CAPTURE @PROJECT_VERSION@" "OCTA-CAPTURE Manual"
.SH NAME
octa\-pulse\-pairs \- manage native PulseAudio stereo pairs and rate changes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBocta-pulse-pairs\fR [\fB\-\-install\fR | \fB\-\-watch\fR | \fB\-\-packaged-service\fR | \fB\-\-rate\fR HZ]
                 [\fB\-\-device\fR CARD] [\fB\-\-bin-dir\fR DIR] [\fB\-\-help\fR]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reconcile the OCTA-CAPTURE stereo-pair profile with its current hardware rate.
Native PulseAudio is required for coordinated rate changes.
At 44.1/48/96 kHz there are five playback and six recording stereo pairs;
Recording 11-12 is the Mixer A return. At 192 kHz only pairs 1-2 and 3-4 remain.
.PP
The default device is hw:CARD=OCTACAPTURE.
\fB\-\-rate\fR briefly pauses affected PulseAudio streams, changes the hardware rate,
then restores pair assignments, endpoint/client volumes and mutes.
Stop streams on unavailable higher pairs before requesting 192 kHz.
Direct ALSA clients must release their own streams; PipeWire coordination is unverified.
.PP
\fB\-\-watch\fR watches for present devices.
\fB\-\-install\fR installs and starts the regular-user service.
\fB\-\-packaged-service\fR is the packaged user-service entry point and retires its exact legacy unit.
These operations may briefly interrupt device audio.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; nonzero indicates a usage, device or operation error.
.SH SEE ALSO
octa-capture(1), octa-status(1), octa-preset(1)
